# Signing, for a release APK. Copy this file to keystore.properties next to it
# and fill it in. That file is gitignored and never leaves your machine — the
# key and its password are yours, and nothing in this repository should ever
# contain either.
#
# Without keystore.properties the release build still runs and produces an
# UNSIGNED apk, which is useful for checking that shrinking did not break
# anything and which no device will install.
#
# Make a key once, and keep it forever: an APK signed with a different key
# cannot update one signed with this one. Users would have to uninstall first,
# and the Play Store will not accept the swap at all.
#
#   keytool -genkeypair -v \
#     -keystore aquaplay.jks \
#     -alias aquaplay \
#     -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000
#
# It will ask for a password and a few details; only the password matters.
# Put the .jks somewhere outside this repository — C:/keys/ or ~/keys/ — and
# back it up somewhere you will still have in five years.

storeFile=C:/keys/aquaplay.jks
storePassword=
keyAlias=aquaplay
keyPassword=
